{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQK3JxJkhFdXsqiyGgju","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014eHH4yHv5ccxXoBgWo2U5n","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd .. && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na='This request path is off until part B of #255: the merger\\'s `Rounds` dependency stays unset in `servecmd`, so a conflict, like a red required check, still goes to `ard:needs-human`.'\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,'''`servecmd` wires the review fix loop into the merger as `Rounds`, so a conflict starts a conflict round. In it the controller fetches `main` itself, trial-merges it into a scratch worktree (no commit, attributes from the empty tree, no rerere, renormalize or `-X`), and gives the worker an untrusted `conflict.md` (capped, escaped paths; no hunks). The first agent step starts with that merge in its worktree. After the step the controller runs no git in the agent's worktree: it reads the recorded conflicted files for leftover markers (advisory), measures the PR's own diff against the fetched `main` tip, not the job's base, and hands the committer the full diff against `main` with `MergeParent` set to that tip. The code lane does not run `git merge`: it fetches `main` into a private ref and refuses unless it equals `MergeParent` (`ErrMergeParent`), requires the branch still at the job's base (`ErrConflict`, no retry), writes the declared files over main's tree, and checks that the result differs from `main` only in declared paths that pass `CheckCodePath`, so `.github/`, `.ard/`, `.gitmodules` and `.gitattributes` equal `main` byte for byte. It commits with parents `[branch tip, main tip]` and pushes with a lease on the branch tip (a merge whose tree equals main's is still committed). A GitHub rejection of a merge that brings in workflow changes ends `needs-human`. The loop counts a conflict round as landed only when the head is a merge that includes the round's head and whose second parent is on `main`. The conflict-round section of the worker prompt is a separate human PR.''')\nb='once the merger\\'s `Rounds` dependency is wired (part B of #255; unset today), it becomes'\nassert b in s\ns=s.replace(b,'with the merger\\'s `Rounds` dependency wired in `servecmd` (#255), it becomes')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Rounds\" docs/*.md | grep -i \"unset\\|part B\" | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10196,"cache_read_input_tokens":107448,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10196},"output_tokens":54,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bbc59d5-e782-4f96-8016-808f1442da36","uuid":"26bfb490-fca1-4048-95a8-b08f04239f79","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:54:41.886Z","request_id":"req_011ChQK3HjNYqT7DmDVyfo95"}
