{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQK9Pyai6dtaiErCUEx4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Part B is implemented, but I did not write the end-to-end conflict-round test with the fakes, which the issue lists under \"Done when\".\n\nThe `go test` runs for gitx, committer, effects, worker, reviewfix, merger and servecmd pass. `TestTransientCancelledInBackoff` failed once in a full committer run and passed on rerun. `make lint` stops on gofmt of a testdata file I didn't touch: `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **gitx:**\n  - `MergeNoCommit` and `MergeAbort` run hardened merges.\n  - `CommitOp.Parents` is the full parent list, rather than extra parents beyond HEAD as the plan said.\n- **committer:**\n  - `CodeRequest.MergeParent` and `ErrMergeParent` are new, and the merge path is in `internal/committer/merge.go`.\n  - The lane runs no `git merge`. It fetches `main` into a private ref and refuses unless that equals `MergeParent`.\n  - The branch must still be at the job's base, and there is no retry.\n  - It writes the declared files over main's tree, and every difference from main must be a declared path that passes `CheckCodePath`.\n  - It commits with parents [branch tip, main tip] and pushes with a lease.\n- **worker:**\n  - `conflict.go` builds a capped, escaped `conflict.md` and fetches main itself.\n  - The merge is done before the first agent step, and no git runs in the agent's worktree afterwards.\n  - Leftover conflict markers are checked in the recorded conflicted files (advisory only).\n  - The diff guard measures against the fetched main tip.\n  - A push rejected over workflow changes ends as needs-human.\n- **reviewfix and servecmd:** `mergeIncludes` also requires the second parent to be an ancestor of main. The review fix loop is now passed to the merger as `Rounds`.\n- **docs:** `docs/proposal.md` is updated.\n\nGaps and deviations:\n- **Missing tests:** there are no worker tests for `conflictInput`, the conflict-mode diff guard or the workflow-rejection hold. The planned non-lease-push and dry-run committer tests are also missing. The committer's merge tests pass.\n- **Thinner `conflict.md`:** it lists the conflicted paths and change counts for each side, with no hunks or commit summaries.\n- **Looser parent check:** the second-parent check is \"ancestor of main\", not strict first-parent history.\n- **Workflow hold:** it matches the word \"workflow\" in the push error text.\n- **Not done:** there was no starter-config switch to turn on, since those files are protected. The worker prompt's conflict section is still the separate human PR.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/323/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1413,"cache_read_input_tokens":119712,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1413},"output_tokens":754,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bbc59d5-e782-4f96-8016-808f1442da36","uuid":"646d0e73-e149-4c07-b0fc-e8408d22e966","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:56:03.254Z","request_id":"req_011ChQK9PqQWyBFUAnKgZmRK"}
